# Framework-managed transient state — uncommitted by design.
# The build session's in-flight checkpoint log (see STAGE-PROMPT-PROTOCOL
# <status_log>). Read by an orchestrator consultation; cleared at stage close.
.claude/build-status.md

# The session's current role (work / verifier / orchestrator / refactor). Local to
# the machine; not part of the project's shared state. `.claude/role` is the ONLY
# marker written or read — its compatibility alias was retired. The retired name stays
# listed below on purpose: nothing writes it any more, but a project that predates the
# removal can still have one on disk, and it must never be committable.
.claude/role
.claude/active-mode

# PROC-001 red-gate markers (shipped via the red-gate hook): the open-stage marker
# and the per-stage red-approval marker. Per-session, never committed. Comments stay
# on their OWN lines — an inline `#` becomes part of the pattern and ignores nothing.
.claude/stage-active
.claude/red-approved

# Build-receipt event ledgers (per-session JSONL written by the receipts
# machinery; local observability data, never committed).
.claude/receipts/

# Build-receipt reports (rendered JSON/HTML/MD views written by
# `node scripts/build-receipts.cjs render`; local observability output). This
# entry is a default, not a wall — a report you want to keep is deliberately
# trackable: negate or delete this line for the files you commit.
reports/

